meta {
  name: Update Lead
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/leads/{{leadId}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "status": "Contacted",
    "temperature": "Warm",
    "leadSourceId": "{{mailerLeadSourceId}}"
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("echoes the changed fields in canonical form", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("id");
    expect(body.status).to.equal("Contacted");
    expect(body.temperature).to.equal("Warm");
    expect(body.leadSource.label).to.equal("Mailer");
    expect(body.leadSource.id).to.equal(bru.getVar("mailerLeadSourceId"));
  });

  test("bumps lastActivityAt", function () {
    expect(res.getBody()).to.have.property("lastActivityAt");
  });

  test("returns only the patchable fields, not a whole LeadDetail", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.not.have.property("household");
    expect(body).to.not.have.property("activities");
    expect(body).to.not.have.property("latestQuoteRecap");
  });
}

docs {
  # PATCH /leads/:id — Lead Detail inline edits (PAC-38)

  Status, temperature and lead source, edited in place from `/leads/:id`. Each
  Select on the page fires one field; every field is optional and the body must
  not be empty.

  - **Module:** `leads`
  - **Permission:** `leads:write`
  - **Data scope:** identical clamp to `GET /leads/:id` —
    `LeadAccessService.loadOwnedLead` runs **before** anything is written, so
    another producer's lead is a `404` and is never modified.

  ## Path params
  | param | type   | notes                                               |
  |-------|--------|-----------------------------------------------------|
  | id    | string | ObjectId. A malformed id is a `404`, never a `500`. |

  ## Body
  | field          | type   | rules                                                        |
  |----------------|--------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
  | status         | enum   | a canonical `LEAD_STATUSES` label — raw codes are rejected   |
  | temperature    | enum   | `Hot` \| `Warm` \| `Cold`. **`Unknown` is not accepted.**    |
  | leadSourceId   | string | a row id from `GET /lead-sources`, or `__none__` to clear it |

  At least one must be present; `{}` is a `400`.

  ## Behaviour worth knowing

  **`leadSourceId` is the point of this endpoint.** Leads that arrive through a
  public share link (PAC-37) carry no source — nobody has said where they came
  from yet. Without this control those leads could never be corrected. Sending
  `__none__` unsets it again, so a mis-attributed lead can be returned to "not
  known yet" and will again match the `GET /leads?leadSourceId=__none__` filter.

  **Only an active source this agency can see is accepted**, matching
  `POST /leads`: a well-formed id that is archived, belongs to another agency,
  or does not exist is a `400`. An archived source stays on the records that
  already carry it — it just cannot be picked again.

  **`Unknown` temperature is not selectable.** It is the display state of a lead
  nobody has assessed, not a choice — mirroring `LEAD_TEMPERATURE_OPTIONS`.

  **Status is not forward-only.** Unlike the automatic advance the Quote and
  Sold forms perform, this accepts any canonical label in any direction: a
  producer correcting a mis-clicked `Sold` back to `Requote` is a real
  operation, and a one-way control would strand the record.

  **`lastActivityAt` is always bumped**, so the row moves to the top of the
  Leads list afterwards. The list sorts on it and an edit *is* activity —
  intended, not a bug.

  **No activity row is written.** None of the `ACTIVITY_TYPES` members means
  "status changed"; adding one is a follow-up, not a side effect of this
  endpoint.

  ## Response `200`
  ```json
  {
    "id": "665f...ac1",
    "status": "Contacted",
    "temperature": "Warm",
    "leadSource": { "id": "66f0…a1", "label": "Mailer" },
    "lastActivityAt": "2026-08-04T09:15:44.120Z"
  }
  ```

  Only the fields the patch can change are returned, in their server-canonical
  form — re-running the ten-collection `GET /leads/:id` assembly on every
  dropdown change would make an inline edit cost more than the page load. The
  client writes these four values straight into its cached `LeadDetail`.

  ## Errors
  - `400 Bad Request` — empty body, an unknown status, `temperature: "Unknown"`,
    or a lead-source code that is not selectable.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — missing/expired access token.
  - `403 Forbidden` — `leads` module disabled, or missing `leads:write` (a
    read-only user gets this).
  - `404 Not Found` — no such lead, a malformed id, or a lead outside scope.
}
